    <section class="oop-section" id="class-object">
      <h2>1. <LocalizedText sk="Čo je trieda a objekt?" en="What are a class and an object?" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText
        sk="Trieda (class) je predpis, ktorý určuje, aké údaje a správanie budú mať jej objekty. Objekt je konkrétna inštancia triedy. Z jednej triedy môžeš vytvoriť veľa objektov s rôznymi hodnotami."
        en="A class is a blueprint that defines the data and behavior its objects have. An object is a particular instance of that class. One class can create many objects with different values."
      /></p>
      <div class="oop-concept-grid">
        <article class="oop-concept-card">
          <h3><LocalizedText sk="Trieda" en="Class" /></h3>
          <p><LocalizedText sk="Opisuje spoločné vlastnosti a operácie, napríklad názov a schopnosť hovoriť." en="Describes shared properties and operations, such as a name and the ability to speak." /></p>
        </article>
        <article class="oop-concept-card">
          <h3><LocalizedText sk="Objekt" en="Object" /></h3>
          <p><LocalizedText sk="Konkrétny prípad triedy, napríklad pes s menom Rex." en="A particular instance of a class, such as a dog named Rex." /></p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Dog:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name

    def speak(self) -> str:
        return f"{self.name} says woof"


first_dog = Dog("Rex")
second_dog = Dog("Luna")

print(first_dog.speak())
print(second_dog.speak())`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>Rex says woof
Luna says woof</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="first_dog a second_dog sú dva rôzne objekty rovnakej triedy Dog. Každý má vlastnú hodnotu atribútu name." en="first_dog and second_dog are two different objects of the same Dog class. Each has its own name attribute value." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="init-self">
      <h2>2. <code>__init__</code> <LocalizedText sk="a" en="and" /> <code>self</code></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="__init__ sa automaticky zavolá pri vytváraní novej inštancie a nastaví jej počiatočný stav. Parameter self odkazuje na konkrétny objekt, s ktorým metóda pracuje. Pri vytváraní objektu triedy Dog parameter self nepíšeš ručne — Python ho odovzdá automaticky." en="__init__ is called when a new instance is created and sets its initial state. The self parameter refers to the particular object the method works with. When creating a Dog object, you do not pass self manually — Python supplies it automatically." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class User:
    def __init__(self, username: str, active: bool = True) -> None:
        self.username = username
        self.active = active


user = User("daniel")
print(user.username)
print(user.active)`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>daniel
True</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Názov __init__ začína aj končí dvoma podčiarkovníkmi. Je to špeciálna metóda Pythonu, nie bežná funkcia, ktorú treba volať samostatne." en="The name __init__ starts and ends with two underscores. It is a special Python method, not a regular function you should call separately." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="attributes-methods">
      <h2>3. <LocalizedText sk="Atribúty a metódy" en="Attributes and methods" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Atribúty uchovávajú stav objektu. Metódy definujú správanie, ktoré súvisí s týmto stavom. Atribút vytvorený cez self v __init__ je zvyčajne atribútom inštancie — každý objekt má svoju hodnotu." en="Attributes store an object's state. Methods define behavior related to that state. An attribute assigned through self in __init__ is usually an instance attribute, so each object has its own value." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Counter:
    def __init__(self, start: int = 0) -> None:
        self.value = start

    def increment(self) -> None:
        self.value += 1

    def reset(self) -> None:
        self.value = 0


counter_a = Counter()
counter_b = Counter(10)
counter_a.increment()
print(counter_a.value)
print(counter_b.value)`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>1
10</pre>
      </div>
      <h3><LocalizedText sk="Atribút inštancie a atribút triedy" en="Instance attribute and class attribute" /></h3>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Atribút triedy sa definuje priamo v triede a zdieľajú ho inštancie, pokiaľ ho neprekryjú vlastným atribútom. Je vhodný napríklad pre konštantu. Zdieľaný meniteľný zoznam však býva častou chybou." en="A class attribute is defined on the class and is shared by instances unless an instance shadows it. It can be useful for a constant. A shared mutable list, however, is a common bug." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Team:
    # Shared constant: suitable as a class attribute.
    sport = "football"

    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name
        self.members: list[str] = []  # A separate list per object.`} />
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Ak sa má zoznam meniť nezávisle pre každý objekt, vytvor ho v __init__ pomocou self.members = []. Nedefinuj ho ako members = [] priamo v tele triedy." en="If the list must change independently for each object, create it in __init__ using self.members = []. Do not define it as members = [] directly in the class body." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="inheritance">
      <h2>4. <LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť a super()" en="Inheritance and super()" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť vyjadruje vzťah „je typom“ (is-a). Podtrieda preberá rozhranie a správanie nadradenej triedy a môže ho rozšíriť alebo upraviť. super() umožňuje zavolať implementáciu nadradenej triedy bez pevného pomenovania jej názvu." en="Inheritance represents an “is-a” relationship. A subclass reuses the parent class interface and behavior and can extend or override it. super() calls the parent implementation without hard-coding its name." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Person:
    def __init__(self, name: str) -> None:
        self.name = name

    def introduce(self) -> str:
        return f"My name is {self.name}."


class Student(Person):
    def __init__(self, name: str, student_id: str) -> None:
        super().__init__(name)
        self.student_id = student_id

    def introduce(self) -> str:
        base_intro = super().introduce()
        return f"{base_intro} Student ID: {self.student_id}."


student = Student("Anna", "B123")
print(student.introduce())`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>My name is Anna. Student ID: B123.</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="oop-note"><LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť použi vtedy, keď podtrieda naozaj predstavuje špecializovaný typ nadradenej triedy. Nevytváraj dedičnosť len preto, aby si zdieľal niekoľko riadkov kódu." en="Use inheritance when the subclass genuinely is a specialized type of the parent. Do not introduce inheritance just to share a few lines of code." /></p>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="composition">
      <h2>5. <LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia: objekt používa iný objekt" en="Composition: an object uses another object" /></h2>
      <p><LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia vyjadruje vzťah „má“ (has-a). Trieda obsahuje alebo používa iné objekty namiesto toho, aby od nich dedila. Kurz napríklad obsahuje zoznam študentov; kurz nie je typom študenta." en="Composition represents a “has-a” relationship. A class contains or uses other objects instead of inheriting from them. A course, for example, contains a list of students; a course is not a type of student." /></p>
      <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Course:
    def __init__(self, title: str) -> None:
        self.title = title
        self.students: list[Student] = []

    def enroll(self, student: Student) -> None:
        self.students.append(student)

    def student_count(self) -> int:
        return len(self.students)


# Reuse the Student class from the inheritance example above.
course = Course("Python Basics")
course.enroll(Student("Anna", "B123"))
course.enroll(Student("Peter", "B124"))
print(course.title)
print(course.student_count())`} />
      <div class="oop-output">
        <strong><LocalizedText sk="Výstup" en="Output" /></strong>
        <pre>Python Basics
2</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="oop-comparison-table-wrap">
        <table class="oop-comparison-table">
          <thead><tr><th><LocalizedText sk="Dedičnosť" en="Inheritance" /></th><th><LocalizedText sk="Kompozícia" en="Composition" /></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><LocalizedText sk="„Je typom“ — Student je Person." en="“Is-a” — a Student is a Person." /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="„Má“ — Course má študentov." en="“Has-a” — a Course has students." /></td></tr>
            <tr><td><LocalizedText sk="Použi na špecializáciu existujúceho typu." en="Use to specialize an existing type." /></td><td><LocalizedText sk="Použi na skladanie správania z spolupracujúcich objektov." en="Use to compose behavior from collaborating objects." /></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="mistakes">
      <h2>6. <LocalizedText sk="Typické chyby" en="Common mistakes" /></h2>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="Chyba 1: zabudnutý self" en="Mistake 1: missing self" /></h3>
        <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Greeter:
    def greet():
        return "Hello"

# greet expects no instance parameter, but Python supplies one:
# Greeter().greet() raises TypeError.`} />
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Oprava: pri bežnej inštančnej metóde uveď self ako prvý parameter." en="Fix: include self as the first parameter of a normal instance method." /></p>
        <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Greeter:
    def greet(self) -> str:
        return "Hello"

print(Greeter().greet())`} />
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="Chyba 2: zdieľaný meniteľný atribút" en="Mistake 2: shared mutable attribute" /></h3>
        <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Group:
    members: list[str] = []  # Shared by all instances!`} />
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Oprava: inicializuj zoznam v __init__, aby mal každý objekt vlastný zoznam." en="Fix: initialize the list in __init__ so every object gets its own list." /></p>
        <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Group:
    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.members: list[str] = []`} />
      </div>
      <div class="oop-mistake">
        <h3><LocalizedText sk="Chyba 3: podtrieda neinicializuje nadradenú časť" en="Mistake 3: subclass skips parent initialization" /></h3>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Ak nadradená trieda nastavuje potrebné atribúty v __init__, podtrieda má spravidla zavolať super().__init__(...). Inak môžu atribúty chýbať alebo objekt nebude inicializovaný podľa očakávania." en="If a parent class sets required attributes in __init__, the subclass should usually call super().__init__(...). Otherwise, attributes may be missing or the object may not be initialized as expected." /></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section" id="practice">
      <h2>7. <LocalizedText sk="Úloha na precvičenie" en="Practice task" /></h2>
      <div class="oop-task-card">
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Vytvor triedu Book s atribútmi title, author a pages. Pridaj metódu summary(), ktorá vráti krátky opis knihy, a metódu is_long(), ktorá vráti True, ak má kniha aspoň 300 strán. Vytvor dva objekty a vypíš ich opisy aj výsledok is_long()." en="Create a Book class with title, author, and pages attributes. Add a summary() method that returns a short description and an is_long() method that returns True when the book has at least 300 pages. Create two objects and print their summaries and is_long() results." /></p>
        <p><strong><LocalizedText sk="Najprv to skús samostatne. Riešenie si otvor až potom." en="Try it yourself first. Open the solution only afterwards." /></strong></p>
        <details class="oop-solution">
          <summary><LocalizedText sk="Zobraziť vzorové riešenie" en="Show sample solution" /></summary>
          <CopyCodeBlock code={`class Book:
    def __init__(self, title: str, author: str, pages: int) -> None:
        if pages <= 0:
            raise ValueError("pages must be positive")
        self.title = title
        self.author = author
        self.pages = pages

    def summary(self) -> str:
        return f"{self.title} by {self.author} ({self.pages} pages)"

    def is_long(self) -> bool:
        return self.pages >= 300


book_a = Book("Clean Code", "Robert C. Martin", 464)
book_b = Book("Small Python Guide", "A. Novak", 120)
print(book_a.summary())
print(book_a.is_long())
print(book_b.summary())
print(book_b.is_long())`} />
          <div class="oop-output">
            <strong><LocalizedText sk="Očakávaný výstup" en="Expected output" /></strong>
            <pre>Clean Code by Robert C. Martin (464 pages)
True
Small Python Guide by A. Novak (120 pages)
False</pre>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oop-section oop-self-check" id="self-check">
      <h2><LocalizedText sk="Rýchla kontrola porozumenia" en="Quick self-check" /></h2>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="1. Aký je rozdiel medzi triedou a objektom?" en="1. What is the difference between a class and an object?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Trieda je definícia typu; objekt je konkrétna inštancia tejto triedy." en="A class defines a type; an object is a particular instance of that class." /></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="2. Prečo je self prvým parametrom inštančnej metódy?" en="2. Why is self the first parameter of an instance method?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Odkazuje na objekt, na ktorom sa metóda volá, takže metóda vie čítať a meniť jeho atribúty." en="It refers to the object the method is called on, allowing the method to read and change that object's attributes." /></p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary><LocalizedText sk="3. Kedy je vhodnejšia kompozícia než dedičnosť?" en="3. When is composition preferable to inheritance?" /></summary>
        <p><LocalizedText sk="Keď objekt používa alebo obsahuje iný objekt („má“), ale nie je jeho špecializovaným typom („je“)." en="When an object uses or contains another object (“has-a”) but is not a specialized type of it (“is-a”)." /></p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <footer class="oop-footer-note">
      <p><strong><LocalizedText sk="Poznámka k rozsahu materiálu" en="Note about the scope" /></strong></p>
